From f18140fa535314e8f24da5ef3e9541a0f1fe3326 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: egeorgan <evangelos.georganas@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:29:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] remote backend: several sequences, one engine slot each
 (llama-server -np N)

With n_seq_max > 1 the client asks the engine for its slots (k3 --serve-slots N) and maps
sequence s to slot s: per-slot lengths and checkpoint positions, seq_rm/seq_pos_* per
sequence, seq_cp as a whole-sequence COPY, seq_keep and clear reset the other slots.
decode_remote groups a batch by sequence and sends it as one DECODE_MULTI request, so the
engine decodes the sequences' single tokens together; long prompt segments still go first
as a separate head so the engine checkpoints before the assistant header. Logits rows are
returned in batch order. With one sequence the requests are those of before.
